        "date_added": "2026-10-25 02:58:27",
        "twitter_handle": null,
        "display_name": null,
        "comment": "Static analysis and structural caveat for this fresh community ARM ELF, 2026-10-24 America/New_York. SHA-256 verified; sample never executed. At file offset 0x109b8 the XOR-0x26 string decrypts to devs.homelabnode.qzz.io. Declared section layout contains table_key 0x08f39449, whose four bytes XOR to 0x26; table unlock routine 0xec4c applies those key bytes. Main unlocks entries 0-3, resolves the host table and stores a selected address into sockaddr. At 0xe1cc-0xe1d8, mvn 0x2080 followed by subtract 0x13 yields halfword 0xdf6c: ARM little-endian memory 6c df gives network-order port 27871. Related SPARC sample d332dc8d033bf9687075a977ec3120bee7fcc4586592cc986fd432bb5525f7bc independently constructs port 0x6cdf and has the identical encrypted domain. Important limitation: this ARM file has a four-byte discrepancy between writable-section file offsets and their PT_LOAD-derived offsets. Configuration above is decoded from declared section layout; runtime viability is unverified. Preserve this anomaly rather than silently repairing/reuploading it or treating it as a distinct working bot variant. No repaired executable was written, no execution and no C2 TCP contact."
      }
